<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Scharrig half yr shr up, div steady.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Scharrig half yr shr up, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		    5.7	 vs    1.4</p>
<p>    Div, (cts)		  2.0	 vs    2.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     7.75	vs    1.91</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     8.18	vs    2.25</p>
<p>    Tax			   0.57	vs    0.34</p>
<p>    Finance charges	   9.29	vs    4.08</p>
<p>    Turnover		  107.06	vs   98.42</p>
<p>Full name: Scharrig Mining Ltd</p>
<p>Div payable: Nov 14</p>
<p>On register: Oct 17</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that due to production requirements for the second half, turnover should increase as well as profitability. Contract awards on tenders for larger projects outside the current client base, would result in better overall ustilisation of plant, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
<p>e-mail: johannesburg.newsroom@reuters.com</p>
